# TODO - Source formatting contract

## Objective

Enforce the existing root formatting configurations.

## Acceptance

- Check all authored text files for the 80-character line limit.
- Keep generated, binary and local user data outside authored-text checks.
- Keep the current linter rules; do not weaken checks to pass validation.

## Evidence

Fresh `cargo validate --no-cache` passes with the width check on all
discovered authored text, in addition to the existing Rustfmt, Clippy and
MarkdownLint configuration. The diagnostic includes the file and line.

Tests cover the 80/81 Unicode-character boundary, invalid source encoding,
binary bytes, the generated Cargo.lock and ignored local directories.
Only reviewed direct roadmap links with their explicit marker and the
existing MarkdownLint schema identifier may exceed the width limit.
A generic marker cannot exempt other authored prose or files.
